#v(0.8cm)

#fc-steps(
  ([Add data], [Put the original files in `data/raw/` and never touch them again.
    Lookups and crosswalks go in `data/misc/`.]),
  ([Clean], [Write and run `{dataset}_clean.R`. It saves one
    `data/clean/{dataset}.rds` and does nothing else.]),
  ([Analyse], [Run `{dataset}_analyse_{topic}.R`. It reads the `.rds` and writes
    plots, tables and inline numbers into `output/`.]),
  ([Write & compile], [Write the text in `typst/main.typ`, which pulls in the plots,
    tables and numbers. Preview and export it in Positron or VS Code. Compiling is
    instant: nothing is computed.]),
)

#v(0.8cm)
#line(length: 100%, stroke: 0.5pt + border)
#text(size: 9pt, fill: gray.darken(20%))[
  *The report* (`typst/main.pdf`) is the only real output. Everything in between can be
  regenerated by re-running the scripts, which is why it isn't committed to git. \
  *The clean data* is a checkpoint: once it exists, you only re-run the clean script if
  you find a problem with the cleaning. Analysis scripts never re-clean. \
  Next page: the full chain in detail. After that: the folder structure. \
  Details and conventions: `docs/Template manual.md`.
]

